y>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EBARA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SERIKAWA, ROBERTO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SU, QINGQUAN</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISAKA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA TATSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SERIKAWA ROBERTO MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SU QINGQUAN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SERIKAWA, ROBERTO, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SU, QINGQUAN</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A hydrothermal electrolysis apparatus characterized in that it is equipped with a reaction chamber for electrolyzing a material to be treated under a high pressure at a high temperature and the total surface area of a pair of electrodes disposed in the reaction chamber (31) is 0.05 m&lt;2&gt; or more per m&lt;3&gt; of the volume of the material to be treated; a hydrothermal electrolysis apparatus characterized in that it has two or more of cylindrical reaction chambers, each having an inner metal wall acting as a cathode, and anodes are disposed within the reaction chamber; and a hydrothermal electrolysis method characterized as comprising incorporating conducting particles into the material to be treated, to thereby substantially increase the surface area of electrodes in hydrothermal electrolysis are disclosed as some embodiments of the present invention. Such apparatuses and methods for hydrothermal electrolysis can be used for treating a large amount of liquid wastes with good efficiency.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce dispositif d'électrolyse hydrothermique se caractérise par le fait qu'il est équipé d'une chambre de réaction servant à électrolyser une substance à traiter sous haute pression et à des températures élevées et par le fait que la surface utile totale de deux électrodes se trouvant dans la chambre de réaction (31) est de 0,05 m&lt;2&gt; ou plus par m&lt;3&gt; de volume de la substance à traiter. Ce dispositif se caractérise également par le fait qu'il est équipé de deux chambres de réaction cylindriques, ou plus, dont la paroi intérieure de chacune fait office de cathode, les anodes étant placées à l'intérieur de ladite chambre de réaction. Le procédé d'électrolyse hydrothermique se caractérise par le fait que l'on incorpore des particules conductrices dans la substance à traiter, afin d'augmenter sensiblement la surface utile des électrodes. Plusieurs modes de réalisation de cette invention font appel à cette technique. Ces dispositifs et les procédés correspondants d'électrolyse hydrothermique permettent de traiter une grande quantité de déchets liquides et ce, de manière des plus satisfaisante.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>